# Patch 0920 (device test of DevJunior, 12.11.2026: skin v14 "comes out like this", every texture of Leon colourful
# noise, with Vulkan as with GLES). Not a bug of the prototype: a port fix for the mods' place of patch 0914.
# The graphics processor sees the mods' place at the physical addresses 0x04000000..0x057FFFFF (re4_gx_physical,
# runtime/mod_place.cpp), but the texture registers kept the GameCube's 21 bits of address / 32 (64 MB): a texture,
# palette or preload from the place wrapped to 0x00000000.. and the decoder read MEM1 there. The registers' 24-bit
# value has room (bits 21..23 are unused on the GameCube): GXInitTexObj, GXInitTexObjData, GXInitTlutObj and the
# preloads write 24 bits, the getters read 24; runtime/gx_decode.cpp (bindMap, tlutLoad) reads 24 bits. Every address
# below 64 MB keeps its value.
--- a/src/lib/GXTexture.c
+++ b/src/lib/GXTexture.c
@@ -229,7 +229,7 @@
     SET_REG_FIELD(648, t->image0, 4, 20, format & 0xF);
     ASSERTMSGLINEV(654, ((u32)image_ptr & 0x1F) == 0, "%s: %s pointer not aligned to 32B", "GXInitTexObj", "image");
     imageBase = (re4_gx_physical(image_ptr) >> 5) & 0x01FFFFFF; /* port: patch 0031 */
-    SET_REG_FIELD(656, t->image3, 21, 0, imageBase);
+    SET_REG_FIELD(656, t->image3, 24, 0, imageBase); /* port: patch 0920 */
 
     switch (format & 0xF) {
     case GX_TF_I4:
@@ -338,7 +338,7 @@
     CHECK_GXBEGIN(837, "GXInitTexObjData");
     ASSERTMSGLINEV(840, ((u32)image_ptr & 0x1F) == 0, "%s: %s pointer not aligned to 32B", "GXInitTexObjData", "image");
     imageBase = (re4_gx_physical(image_ptr) >> 5) & 0x01FFFFFF; /* port: patch 0031 */
-    SET_REG_FIELD(843, t->image3, 21, 0, imageBase);
+    SET_REG_FIELD(843, t->image3, 24, 0, imageBase); /* port: patch 0920 */
 }
 
 void GXInitTexObjWrapMode(GXTexObj* obj, GXTexWrapMode sm, GXTexWrapMode tm) {
@@ -465,7 +465,7 @@
     const __GXTexObjInt* t = (const __GXTexObjInt *)obj;
 
     ASSERTMSGLINE(1095, obj, "Texture Object Pointer is null");
-    *image_ptr = (void *)(GET_REG_FIELD(t->image3, 21, 0) << 5);
+    *image_ptr = (void *)(GET_REG_FIELD(t->image3, 24, 0) << 5); /* port: patch 0920 */
     *width = (u32)GET_REG_FIELD(t->image0, 10, 0) + 1;
     *height = (u32)GET_REG_FIELD(t->image0, 10, 10) + 1;
     *format = t->fmt;
@@ -478,7 +478,7 @@
     const __GXTexObjInt* t = (const __GXTexObjInt *)to;
 
     ASSERTMSGLINE(1108, to, "Texture Object Pointer is null");
-    return (void*)(GET_REG_FIELD(t->image3, 21, 0) << 5);
+    return (void*)(GET_REG_FIELD(t->image3, 24, 0) << 5); /* port: patch 0920 */
 }
 
 u16 GXGetTexObjWidth(const GXTexObj* to) {
@@ -676,7 +676,7 @@
     ASSERTMSGLINEV(1356, ((u32)lut & 0x1F) == 0, "%s: %s pointer not aligned to 32B", "GXInitTlutObj", "Tlut");
     t->tlut = 0;
     SET_REG_FIELD(1359, t->tlut, 2, 10, fmt);
-    SET_REG_FIELD(1360, t->loadTlut0, 21, 0, re4_gx_physical(lut) >> 5); /* port: patch 0031 */
+    SET_REG_FIELD(1360, t->loadTlut0, 24, 0, re4_gx_physical(lut) >> 5); /* port: patches 0031, 0920 */
     SET_REG_FIELD(1361, t->loadTlut0, 8, 24, 0x64);
     t->numEntries = n_entries;
 }
@@ -685,7 +685,7 @@
     const __GXTlutObjInt* t = (const __GXTlutObjInt *)tlut_obj;
 
     ASSERTMSGLINE(1382, tlut_obj, "TLut Object Pointer is null");
-    *data = (void *)(GET_REG_FIELD(t->loadTlut0, 21, 0) << 5);
+    *data = (void *)(GET_REG_FIELD(t->loadTlut0, 24, 0) << 5); /* port: patch 0920 */
     *format = GET_REG_FIELD(t->tlut, 2, 10);
     *numEntries = t->numEntries;
 }
@@ -694,7 +694,7 @@
     const __GXTlutObjInt* t = (const __GXTlutObjInt *)tlut_obj;
 
     ASSERTMSGLINE(1391, tlut_obj, "TLut Object Pointer is null");
-    return (void *)(GET_REG_FIELD(t->loadTlut0, 21, 0) << 5);
+    return (void *)(GET_REG_FIELD(t->loadTlut0, 24, 0) << 5); /* port: patch 0920 */
 }
 
 GXTlutFmt GXGetTlutObjFmt(const GXTlutObj* tlut_obj) {
@@ -1003,8 +1003,8 @@
 
     loadImage0 = 0;
     SET_REG_FIELD(0, loadImage0, 8, 24, 0x60);
-    base = t->image3 & 0x1FFFFF;
-    SET_REG_FIELD(1831, loadImage0, 21, 0, base);
+    base = t->image3 & 0xFFFFFF; /* port: patch 0920 */
+    SET_REG_FIELD(1831, loadImage0, 24, 0, base);
 
     loadImage1 = 0;
